@@ -0,0 +1,91 @@
+# K718 HALO Phase 1 — source package
+
+This package is intended to be copied over the K718 sketch folder as a bounded firmware patch. It replaces the dashboard/input shell and preserves the existing BLE-MIDI transport and generated K1 map.
+
+## Copy these files into the sketch folder
+
+```bash
+cp JC3636_K718_REMOTED_BLE_V1.ino <SKETCH>/JC3636_K718_REMOTED_BLE_V1.ino
+cp remoted_dashboard.h              <SKETCH>/remoted_dashboard.h
+cp remoted_dashboard.cpp            <SKETCH>/remoted_dashboard.cpp
+cp knob.cpp                         <SKETCH>/knob.cpp
+cp remoted_control.h                <SKETCH>/remoted_control.h
+cp remoted_control.cpp              <SKETCH>/remoted_control.cpp
+cp k718_feedback.h                  <SKETCH>/k718_feedback.h
+cp k718_feedback.cpp                <SKETCH>/k718_feedback.cpp
+cp led_ring_gate.h                  <SKETCH>/led_ring_gate.h
+cp led_ring_gate.cpp                <SKETCH>/led_ring_gate.cpp
+cp battery_gate.cpp                 <SKETCH>/battery_gate.cpp
+cp scr_st77916.h                    <SKETCH>/scr_st77916.h
+```
+
+Do not copy `_stub/` into the Arduino sketch. It exists only so the source package can run a local syntax-surface check outside Arduino.
+
+## What this patch does
+
+- No centre/bullseye value labels.
+- No on-glass link/result/status text.
+- No on-screen 13-dot rim ring.
+- No canned BPM variable or fake beat sweep.
+- No linear row menu.
+- Radial picker is implemented as annular sectors, not a row list.
+- Rotary on home adjusts the active function.
+- Swipe up opens picker.
+- Rotary in picker scrubs sectors.
+- Tap or dwell commits the highlighted sector.
+- Swipe down closes picker.
+- Swipe left/right flips PRI/SEC for per-channel functions.
+- Long press jumps to BRIGHTNESS.
+- `MODE` only sends the 22 enabled ordinals from the locked spec, rendered as numeric ordinals because the generated mode-name table is absent.
+- `PRESET` uses the generated `primary.preset` text count/name table, not a hand-coded 10-slot browser list.
+- BLE-MIDI emits are coalesced: at most one send every 30 ms while rotating, final value after 45 ms quiet.
+- Physical LED ring handles offline/flash feedback; haptic and speaker remain explicit stubs until real drivers are wired.
+
+## Build command
+
+Use the same board target already used by the project:
+
+```bash
+arduino-cli compile \
+  --config-file .arduino-cli.yaml \
+  --libraries ".arduino_build_libs" \
+  --fqbn "esp32:esp32:esp32s3:UploadSpeed=115200,USBMode=hwcdc,CDCOnBoot=cdc,FlashMode=qio,FlashSize=16M,PartitionScheme=huge_app,PSRAM=opi" \
+  "custom/JC3636_K718_REMOTED_BLE_V1"
+```
+
+## Source gates
+
+From this package directory:
+
+```bash
+./run_source_gates.sh
+```
+
+Expected:
+
+```text
+PASS G1
+PASS G2
+PASS G3
+PASS G4
+```
+
+The final gate is still device proof: flash, boot log, idle PERF, interaction PERF, and gesture verification on the K718.
+
+## Required boot tells
+
+Expected boot lines include:
+
+```text
+DASH_INIT halo canvas=360x360 ... fx_mem=INTERNAL|PSRAM_FALLBACK
+MODE_TABLE locked_enabled_count=22 ...
+PRESET_TABLE generated_text_count=5
+K718_FEEDBACK_BRIDGE_STUB haptic=stub speaker=stub led=real
+PERF fps=...
+```
+
+## Known blocks
+
+- Haptic and speaker are still compile-safe stubs; the bridge call sites are present.
+- MEMS mic is not implemented in Phase 1. Centre field is deliberately ambient and not framed as audio- or beat-reactive.
+- Mode names are not invented. The UI renders mode ordinals and sends only the locked enabled ordinals.
